{% from "_section.html.j2" import section_heading %}
{{ section_heading(report, "pages") -}}
{% for card in report.pages %}
<div class="page-card">
  <div class="page-icon">html</div>
  <div class="page-meta">
    <div class="title">{{ card.title }}</div>
    <div class="sub">{{ card.sub_line }}</div>
  </div>
  {% if not single_file %}
  {% if card.static_relpath %}
  <a class="link" href="{{ card.static_relpath }}">static copy →</a>
  {% endif %}
  <a class="link" href="{{ card.link_relpath }}">open →</a>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% if single_file %}
<iframe class="page-frame" title="{{ card.title }}" sandbox="allow-same-origin" srcdoc="{{ card.embed_html }}"></iframe>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if report.pages | selectattr("static_relpath") | list %}
<p class="trunc-note">
  {% if single_file %}
  Notebook pages are embedded as static copies of their outputs, which need no
  network. Interactive elements are drawn as plain HTML, such as a table's rows,
  or named and left out. The interactive marimo pages are in the bundle export
  (<code>ginkgo report</code> without <code>--single-file</code>); they load
  marimo's interface from cdn.jsdelivr.net, so they need a network connection.
  {% else %}
  A marimo page loads marimo's interface from cdn.jsdelivr.net, so it needs a
  network connection to display. Its static copy shows the same outputs offline,
  with interactive elements drawn as plain HTML or named and left out.
  {% endif %}
</p>
{% endif %}
